What is happening is that you need something called a cdf  
environment. It is basically and R package with the name CHIPNAMEcdf,  
like hgu95av2cdf. Affy sees that this package is not installed and  
tries to download and install it for you. Apparently something went  
wrong. You could try downloading the package manually and install it  
yourself from the bioconductor website. There you'll also find a  
listing of existing packages in case you are uncertain about the  
name. Look for "Metadata".

/Kasper


